# The vendored devbin runtime is not this project's to format (Devbin issue
# 0008): a formatting hook that rewrites bin/.devbin/lib/ does so inside an
# install/upgrade commit and breaks the vendored manifest one doctor later.
#
# This project's pre-commit hook chains to Intent's critic gate and stops -- it
# has no prettier pass -- so the fence is insurance here rather than
# load-bearing at commit time. It still lands: a hand `prettier --write` or an
# editor plugin is the other blast radius, and the guarantee should not depend
# on the hook staying the shape it is today.
bin/.devbin/lib/

# Generated views have ONE writer, and it is the renderer. A formatter
# editing these rewrites markup the author wrote, and `intent doctor` then
# reports the drift as a hand-edit on a file nobody touched.
intent/st/steel_threads.md
intent/todo.md
intent/st/*/info.md
intent/st/*/acceptance.md
intent/st/*/WP/*/info.md
intent/issues/*.md
intent/whiteboard/*/wip.md
intent/whiteboard/*/inbox.*.md
